>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be 4D or 5D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 5
>>
Rule 2 (padding must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (stride should be greater than zero)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 > 0
>>
Rule 4 (pad should be at most half of effective kernel size, considering dilation)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= v_1 ≤ (v_2 + (v_2 - 1) * (v_3 - 1)) / 2
>>
Rule 5 (kernel_size, stride and dilation should be greater than zero when they are int)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= v_1 > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0 ∧ v_3 > 0
>>
Rule 6 (if kernel_size is tuple, its length must be 3)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 3
>>
Rule 7 (if stride is None, it defaults to kernel_size)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= if v_1 = v_2 then true else false
>>
Rule 8 (elements in tuple of kernel_size should be positive)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] > 0
>>
Rule 9 (pad value must be less than or equal to kernel_size divided by 2)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 ≤ v_2 / 2
>>
Rule 10 (Input tensor is not complex)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 11 (input tensor should be float or double)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 12 (return_indices should be boolean)
{v_1 : bool} |= v_1 = true ∨ v_1 = false
>>
Rule 13 (If kernel_size is a tuple, then the length of the kernel_size tuple should match the number of spatial dimensions of the input.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tuple(int)} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 then v_2.len = 2 else if ndim(v_1) = 5 then v_2.len = 3 else false
>>
Rule 14 (The number of input channels must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 15 (Effective kernel size must be positive given kernel size and dilation as int)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : int} |= v_1 + (v_1 - 1) * (v_2 - 1) > 0
>>
Rule 16 (Input must be non-empty tensor)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
